  "claim_boundary": [
    "Native-adapter distillation/retention regularization. This does not reproduce Nested Learning, Agent-Dice, or the LoRAGen system.",
    "Two identical heads/new-ABC-latents recipes differ only in the preservation-loss weight: zero versus one. Same source, data order, 128 TRAIN rows per ABC task, learning rates, 512 updates and checkpoints. 30,443,392 trainable parameters per arm; no capacity growth.",
    "Train shared A/B output heads, input/output alignment, layer embeddings, and three new ABC vectors. Freeze shared hidden network and every original task vector.",
    "Preserve all four original task adapters every update: BoolQ, CommonsenseQA, HellaSwag, WinoGrande. Reference the exact untouched native checkpoint using original task vectors. Each task contributes 72 effective 2*B@A matrices. No old evaluation labels or prompts enter optimization.",
    "Loss is mean over four tasks and 72 projections of squared full-matrix error divided by corresponding reference squared norm plus 1e-12. Compute implicit rank16 residual Gram products in FP64 from FP32 factors; this is not factor L2.",
    "Both arms compute all four matrix losses for diagnostics. Only the weight-one arm backpropagates them. Additional matrix gradient computation is accounted for; ABC backbone training exposures and trainable capacity match.",
    "Reference factors and vectors are saved once, hashed, frozen, and checked at checkpoints and completion. Base parameters remain frozen and their full tensor hash is checked per arm and after fresh-process evaluation.",
    "Old behavioral rows remain evaluation-only and are opened for scoring after both arms finish, in a new PID. ABC validation is monitored; no behavioral checkpoint selection.",
    "These are repeated exploratory panels: original Sequence-303 mappings, historical triples, the existing length4 panel, and previously inspected released-task probes. No new independent test-set claim.",
    "Report original-ability retention separately from adapter-specific gain. Prior insertion audit qualified all four starting abilities but only BoolQ for initial adapter gain.",
    "Small effective-matrix error is a training proxy; successful retention requires measured old-task behavior alongside ABC acquisition. No guarantee of preserving unmeasured tasks.",
    "No successful rank8 adapter or privileged reconstructed generator is loaded by either arm."
  ],
